Task: Announcement lifecycle - defect correction
Phase: 1 (Core Accessible Stepping & Semantics)

Two issues, both found by running the built package rather than by assertion.

1. Heel numbering off by one (product defect, fixed).
   createDefaultAnnouncementMessage used currentSegmentIndex + 1. Crossing the
   first heel therefore announced 'Turn 2 reached'. Corrected to the segment
   index now occupied, floored at 1.

   The existing specs could not have caught this: they asserted an announcement
   fired and that message.length > 0. Added specs now assert which turn is named,
   at both the emission and message-builder level.

2. Confirm below threshold (behaviour correct, spec strengthened).
   endGesture below the unlock threshold routes to triggerReset, so progress is
   discarded and state returns to idle. That is exact parity with releasing a
   pointer early. The spec asserted only 'not unlocked' and so passed without
   pinning it; it now asserts state, progress and onReset.

Core suite 158 passed. Demonstration output verified before and after.
